# Direct dependencies and their minimum versions. Edit THIS file, then
# regenerate the lockfile (requirements.txt) under Python 3.14, the version
# the Docker image uses:
#
#   pip install pip-tools
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras \
#       --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# requirements.txt pins every package, direct and transitive, with hashes,
# so builds are reproducible and Dependabot / pip-audit see exact versions.
#
# Production dependencies only. Test, docs and sample-data tools are in
# requirements-dev.in / requirements-dev.txt; for local development install
# both:  pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt

